## 🔐 Android Signing Certificate (Play Store)

For Play Store distribution, you need a separate **Android signing keystore**.  
This is different from the open source software license.

### Generate Release Keystore
```bash
keytool -genkey -v \
  -keystore predictora-release.jks \
  -alias predictora \
  -keyalg RSA \
  -keysize 2048 \
  -validity 10000
```

### Important Keystore Rules
- ⚠️  **NEVER commit the .jks file to Git** — it's in .gitignore
- ⚠️  **Back up your keystore securely** — losing it means you cannot update your app
- Store it in a password manager or secure vault (e.g. AWS Secrets Manager)
- Use GitHub Actions secrets for CI/CD signing (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`)

### Play App Signing (Recommended)
Enroll in **Google Play App Signing** — Google holds your release key in their  
secure infrastructure. You only manage the upload key, reducing the risk of  
losing your signing key.

